  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU Support to Migration Management in Serbia &#x2013; Improving Reception Capacity, Protection Services and Access to Education III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Project aims to support further strengthening and sustainability of protection response to mixed migration in the areas of reception, education, and social protection. The Action is designed to ensure smooth transition of interventions to institutions to enable them to deliver services independently. 
 
Therefore, the Action will continue to support rehabilitation and reconstruction activities, maintenance, procurement of equipment and furniture required to ensure proper and dignified living conditions in government-led centres. 
 
To continue with further strengthening the delivery of essential protection services, including social protection, information and educational services, this Action will support sustainability-oriented, institutional delivery of social protection and educational services, their quality, efficiency, and standardization as foreseen under the national legislative framework and EU/international standards. The Action will also support further capacity building of service providers to increase knowledge and competencies in their priority areas. 
 
The Action will adjust to potential changes in trends throughout project implementation cycle, thus following timely coordination and communication between MoLEVSA, SCRM and IOM. 
In the area of education, the Action focused on strengthening the education system via ensuring professional support for working with migrant children, providing translation of educational material and support for enrolment of students to secondary education.</narrative>
  </description>
